  "finalText": "The new queue is empty. I triaged all 14 weekend tickets, plus 2 more that arrived during the run. It's Monday 2026-03-23, triage time 08:10 UTC. No ticket had company-wide impact, so I didn't open a major incident or page anyone.\n\n**Closed (not service requests):**\n- T-2014: an automatic out-of-office reply.\n- T-2010: a SyncFlow marketing email.\n\n**Merged duplicates (each survivor is the earliest report):**\n- **CRM search errors:** T-2005 merged into T-2004.\n- **Payments builds failing:** T-2012 merged into T-2003.\n- Neither set had a deadline yet, so each survivor got one at triage. Both are now department-wide, sev2, due 12:10.\n- I did not merge the Berlin VPN ticket (T-2001) with the Lisbon one (T-2013). They are different offices with different symptoms, reported days apart.\n\n**Severity, deadline and owner:**\n\n| Ticket | Severity | Due (UTC) | Assigned to |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2001 Berlin VPN drops | sev3 | 23 Mar 17:00 | E-303 (backup cover) |\n| T-2013 Lisbon can't reach VPN | sev2 | 23 Mar 12:10 | E-303 (backup cover) |\n| T-2008 VPN client update fails | sev4 | 26 Mar 17:00 | E-302 |\n| T-2007 Phishing / password entered on a fake page | sev2 (security incident) | 23 Mar 12:10 | E-601 (security on-call) |\n| T-2002 Saved CRM filter gone | sev4 | 26 Mar 17:00 | E-203 (backup cover) |\n| T-2004 CRM search (merged) | sev2 | 23 Mar 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2011 Warehouse overtime missing | sev2 | 23 Mar 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2006 Wrong tax code on payslip | sev2 | 23 Mar 12:10 | E-201 |\n| T-2003 Payments builds (merged) | sev2 | 23 Mar 12:10 | E-101 |\n| T-2009 Build logs page slow | sev4 | 26 Mar 17:00 | E-102 |\n\n**How I set these:**\n- **Severities** come from the escalation matrix, with two exceptions:\n  - T-2006 is sev2 because of the March payroll-close rule in the knowledge base (KB-55), which makes single-user payroll tickets sev2 from 20 to 31 March.\n  - T-2007 is sev2 and goes to security on-call, because the requester typed their password into a fake page.\n- **Deadlines:**\n  - sev1 and sev2 run on the clock from 08:10.\n  - sev3 and sev4 count business hours only, starting when the desk opens at 09:00 and skipping the 25 March holiday.\n- **Leave cover:** the rota put two people on leave on their tickets' deadlines, so the backup rota's on-call engineer took those tickets:\n  - E-301 (VPN), on leave today: E-303 covers.\n  - E-202 (CRM and payroll), on leave 26–27 March: E-203 covers.\n\nI left comments on the tickets explaining these choices.\n\n**Two tickets that arrived during the run:** T-2015 and T-2016 came in at 08:10 Monday, so strictly they aren't weekend tickets. They were in the new queue, so I triaged them by the same rules:\n- **T-2015 (Finance payslips missing):** department-wide payroll, so sev1, due 09:10 today, assigned to E-201. This is the most urgent ticket in the queue.\n- **T-2016 (VPN token app asks to re-register):** sev4, due 26 March 17:00, assigned to E-302.\n\nE-201 now holds four sev2/sev1 tickets due this morning.",
